/-!
# Words for the elementary three-subgroup of McL

The four elements `x`, `y`, `z`, `t` are words in the exact degree-275 ATLAS
permutations. Kernel-checked packed tables certify those word identities,
commutation, and order dividing three. The additional words `u`, `v` are
reserved for the candidate Sylow subgroup in `ThreeRank.Candidate`.

GAP discovered the words, but no GAP assertion is a Lean premise. The original
words and tables, with a reproducible generator, are retained in `source/`.
Source: GLS volume 3, Table 5.3n; ATLAS McLG1-p275B0 (see the carrier module).
-/

@[expose] public section
